* ============================================================================
* memo_ram_hello.dts - owner request 2026-08-11: a students-shaped x64 table
* with a memo field, built entirely in RAM, carrying one memo string.
*
* Why it is built rather than altered: the command surface has CREATE, COPY TO
* and APPEND (blank/many) but no add-a-field-to-an-existing-table verb, and the
* STUDENTS fixture is not mutated by policy. So this creates the same shape
* plus NOTES M in the RAM VFS -- nothing is written to disk.
*
* Incidental re-measurement: MEMO_X64_REOPEN_CANARY_20260513.dts recorded a
* KNOWN-RED behavior -- after CLOSE/USE, an x64 memo field read back as its
* reference token instead of its text, and REPLACE then reported "memo backend
* not attached." Markers H_T2/H_T3 below re-test exactly that on the RAM path.
* If they read .T., that 2026-05-13 red has gone green and the canary needs
* repointing (IDXSTALE precedent).
*
* Run: DO memo_ram_hello  |  regression: REGRESSION RUN MEMO_RAM_HELLO
* Markers: H_T1 (write), H_T2 (reopen readback), H_T3 (update after reopen).
* RUNTIME-PROVEN 2026-08-11 (build 10:05:05): all three .T. on first run --
* the 2026-05-13 reds are GREEN on the RAM path. Promoted per the
* promote-final-tests rule the same day.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

* RAM VFS: DBF + INDEXES under the RAM slot; nothing touches disk.
DO mem
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO mem

FORMULA "MEMO-RAM-HELLO-BEGIN"

* --- students shape + a memo field ------------------------------------------
CREATE X64 STUDMEMO (SID N(8,0), LNAME C(20), FNAME C(15), DOB D, GENDER C(1), MAJOR C(4), ENROLL_D D, GPA N(4,2), EMAIL C(40), NOTES M)
STRUCT

* --- one row, and the memo the owner asked for ------------------------------
APPEND
REPLACE SID WITH 1
REPLACE LNAME WITH "GRIMWOOD"
REPLACE FNAME WITH "DERALD"
REPLACE NOTES WITH "This is a memo test. Hello Memo."
TUPLE NOTES
? "H_T1_memo_written:" + (NOTES = "This is a memo test. Hello Memo.")

* --- residency: table + memo sidecar are RAM files, zero bytes on disk ------
VDISK STATUS

* --- the 2026-05-13 canary case: close, reopen, read the memo back ----------
CLOSE
USE STUDMEMO
TUPLE NOTES
? "H_T2_reopen_readback:" + (NOTES = "This is a memo test. Hello Memo.")

* --- and update after reopen (the second half of the old red) ---------------
REPLACE NOTES WITH "Hello again, memo."
TUPLE NOTES
? "H_T3_update_after_reopen:" + (NOTES = "Hello again, memo.")

FORMULA "MEMO-RAM-HELLO-END"

* --- teardown: drop the RAM disk, restore the x64 disk environment ----------
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
